[539.581512, "o", "**Triggered by the PR watch:** CodeRabbit's review of PR #11 (`orka-demo/quantity-parser`, head `88d6e91`), so I did a full review.\r\n\r\n**Nothing needs you.** Two optional nits for you are at the end.\r\n\r\n### [PR #11](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11): Kubernetes quantity parser\r\n**Status:** Merge state is CLEAN, all checks pass at `418a77b`, there are no approvals, and every review thread is resolved. It didn't need a rebase.\r\n\r\n**What I did**\r\n"]
[539.607537, "o", "- **CodeRabbit's finding was right.** The `M` and `G` suffixes used powers of 1024, so `\"1M\"` came out as 1048576 instead of 1000000. I switched both to powers of 1000 and added tests for `1M`, `1G` and `memory_bytes(\"1G\")`. All three new tests fail on the old code.\r\n- **Pushed** that fix as `418a77b`, a signed and signed-off commit. No backup branch was needed because the push only added a commit.\r\n- **Validation:** the 15 tests pass, pre-commit is clean, and the sandbox test check passed at the new head.\r\n- **Thread:** I replied with the commit and resolved it.\r\n- **Review brief:** [posted](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11#issuecomment-6810034200). It rates the risk Low and asks reviewers one question: nothing calls the module yet, so should it merge now or land with its first caller?\r\n\r\n"]
[539.609796, "o", "**Review totals:** 1 fixed, 0 declined, 0 refuted, 0 pre-existing. My own review found nothing serious beyond CodeRabbit's issue.\r\n\r\n**Optional nits for you**\r\n"]
[539.611674, "o", "1. The parser rejects `1.` and `+1`, which Kubernetes accepts. A test rejects `-1`, so leaving out signs looks deliberate. Either widen the pattern or say so in the module docstring.\r\n"]
[539.717549, "o", "2. The PR description doesn't give the core-logic line count (about 25 lines) under Key Changes. It also doesn't record that a search found no existing parser, not even in `kubernetes-asyncio`. The `pr-checklist` skill asks for both.\r\n\r\n"]
[541.403977, "o", "\r\n===== END REPORT =====\r\n"]
